  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Mississippi received $77.9M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 4,022 awards with an average award size of $19.4K. Obligations fell 98.8% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows much larger totals in prior years: FY22 totaled $5.2B, FY23 totaled $8.8B, FY24 totaled $6.4B, FY25 totaled $8.2B, and FY26 totaled $6.4B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer so far in FY2027 to date, obligating $47.4M. Other top buying agencies include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $8.2M and the Department of Homeland Security with $6.5M. Leading vendors in FY2027 to date include SPATIAL FRONT INC with $6.5M and COLUMBUS MARBLE WORKS, INC. with $5.4M. Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date at $8.9M, followed by All Other Outpatient Care Centers at $7.9M and Computer Systems Design Services at $6.7M. These facts reflect fiscal-year-to-date results and partial current-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2027 to date compared with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 98.8% year over year. Fiscal-year totals in the five prior years were $5.2B in FY22, $8.8B in FY23, $6.4B in FY24, $8.2B in FY25, and $6.4B in FY26 while FY27 shows $77.9M so far. The number of awards in FY2027 to date is 4,022 with an average award size of $19.4K. These figures represent partial fiscal-year-to-date totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $47.4M, making it the largest buyer in FY2027 to date. Top vendors include SPATIAL FRONT INC with $6.5M and COLUMBUS MARBLE WORKS, INC. with $5.4M. Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing leads industries at $8.9M, followed by All Other Outpatient Care Centers at $7.9M and Computer Systems Design Services at $6.7M. These figures are the top-ranked obligations for the fiscal-year-to-date period."
      }
    ]
